{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Do not be agitated on the way.</b> The meaning of רֹגֶז is a term for trembling and commotion. It is said of the overwhelming that comes upon a person from fear: 'a trembling heart' (Deuteronomy 28:65), 'and they trembled and were sick' (ibid. 2:25), 'and trembling under me' (Habakkuk 3:16), 'and your water you shall drink in agitation and in anxiety' (Ezekiel 12:18). Therefore the correct interpretation in my eyes for this verse is that Joseph said to them: Do not be afraid on the way. The matter is that because they were carrying grain, bread, and provisions, and the goods of Egypt, during the days of famine, they might be afraid on the road lest bandits come upon them as they traveled — all the more so on their return with all their property — and they might not hurry on their way. Therefore he told them to walk briskly and hurry to come, as it is said (Genesis 45:9), 'Hurry and go up to my father,' and not to be afraid at all on the road, for his name is upon them — he who rules over all the land of Egypt, and the life of all those lands is in his hand, and from fear of him all will be afraid — and they will go and come in peace:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:45:09.505723981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}